WEBVTT

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.830
Our son's fever isn't coming down.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.290
He's having trouble breathing, too.
I fear that if this keeps up...

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.250
Please, I beg you! Help my son!

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.700
What's all this fuss about, then?

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.000
Please, your lordship! My son is ill!

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.660
Then you should take him
to the doctor in the village.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.910
But, your lordship, the village doctor is not
in tonight, due to his daughter's wedding.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.040
So if I could prevail upon the doctor here...

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.580
You expect <i>my </i>attending doctor
to treat <i>your </i>son?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.120
B-But, your lordship, my son is likely to die!

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.080
So what if he is?

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.910
It's none of my concern what happens
to lowborn folk like you.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:07.160
Burton, I employ you for
your skills as a gardener.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:12.080
But if you mean to trouble me any further...

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.950
Your lordship, I beg of you, as well--

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.950
<i>The mist is hiding the sin</i>

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.700
<i>I hold in my hand the LIST of judgment</i>

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.330
<i>I'm gonna do the perfect crime</i>
<i>and bury them in a cist</i>

00:01:55.330 --> 00:02:00.620
<i>That's my DYING WISH for you</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:06.040
<i>Guys of the privileged class torment the weak</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.120
<i>And they enjoy it</i>

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.660
<i>That's a bloody world, an endlessly</i>
<i>discriminatory society (dystopia)</i>

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:19.660
<i>Happiness does not bloom here</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.790
<i>We are oppressed</i>

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:28.370
<i>We must do something. Come on</i>

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:34.830
<i>Let the end begin</i>

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:40.700
<i>Break it to relieve your soul</i>

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:46.620
<i>Open your eyes. You'll be reborn</i>
<i>when you lose your life</i>

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.700
<i>Lord of crime hora yume no ikenie</i>
<i>We're lords of crime. We're sacrifice for ideals</i>

00:02:51.700 --> 00:03:03.950
<i>Freedom lives forever, even if we die</i>

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:16.000
"A Rare Breed"

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:44.950
Pardon me, but could I trouble you
for directions to Goetsbeck Manor?

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:48.700
Goetsbeck Manor? You wouldn't
happen to be the maths teacher

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.040
we heard was coming to
the university, would you?

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.040
Well, yes. You knew about that?

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.160
You're out in the country now, lad.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:00.870
When an outsider comes to town,
word spreads quickly.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:03.700
On top of which, you come from noble stock,

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.410
but you still teach at the school.
Quite the odd duck.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.250
<i>Not </i>hearing about you would
have been more peculiar.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.450
Peculiar, you say?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:31.540
You'll have to cut that one some slack.
That girl, Michelle, hates aristocrats.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:38.620
After all, the viscount here
as good as let her son die.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:48.620
Ah, Brother! You sure took your time.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.660
I was wandering the streets of the village,
and found myself lost.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:56.540
That sounds like quite the ordeal.
How about we have some tea?

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.660
I'll go and get it ready.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:07.410
It feels as though I've finally come home.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:10.620
"Come home" is a bit out of place, isn't it?

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.540
Other than the quick inspection we made
when we purchased the residence,

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.330
this is your first time coming here, right?

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.330
Indeed, this is no more than
a temporary residence,

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.620
chosen because of its proximity
to the university.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.040
But regardless of where it may be,

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:28.120
any place where I can drink
your tea is home to me.

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.700
Oh, that reminds me...

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.080
Brother, this came for you.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.080
The Viscount of Belfor?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:43.830
Yes. It seems he's the lord
over this whole region.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:50.120
He would like to have us over for dinner
when we have the chance, would he?

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.120
Albert is going to be arriving tonight, right?

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.790
Yes. He is finishing up his current job,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.370
and said he would come
to see how everything was.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:05.500
I see. Then let's all three
of us accept his invitation.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.870
Well, I must say,

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:25.580
Lord Moriarty, I am delighted to have you
and your whole family around my dinner table.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.830
I hope that we, as fellow noblemen,

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:31.250
can enjoy each other's company
for many years to come, as well.

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:33.080
Yes, as do I.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.750
Tonight is a positively smashing evening.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:39.330
I believe I will drink up.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.830
Your lordship, that is plenty.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.700
Hmm? Is it?

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:47.700
Also, it is just about time
for your lordship's medicine.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.410
Is something the matter?

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.500
Oh, just a spot of heart trouble.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.830
Your heart?

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:58.790
Oh, there is no cause for alarm.
Not as long as I have this.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.080
And that is...?

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:07.450
They call it quinine. It was
originally a drug for malaria...

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:12.200
...but from what my personal doctor says,
it's also effective with heart ailments.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.330
Ho?

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:17.200
As it happens, this quinine is homemade.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:22.450
The plant they make it from, quina,
is grown here in my conservatory.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.910
Lord Belfor, is horticulture
one of your interests?

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:30.790
Hmm, in a sense. Collecting rare
plants is a hobby of mine.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:35.660
Indeed. And this hobby of yours
has yielded unexpected benefits.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:44.290
Oh, if you are so inclined, after dinner,
would you like to see my conservatory?

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.250
Yes, by all means.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:54.330
What do you think?

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.870
This is truly a sight to behold.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:05.080
The plants gathered here have different habitats
and growing methods, but they are all rarities.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.200
However, the one thing they all have in common

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:12.410
is that rare breeds can only spring
from the seed of rare breeds.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:15.910
People are quite the same.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:19.290
Don't you agree with me?

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:23.910
Yes, but when you have this much,
it must be a lot of work tending to them.

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:28.000
Oh, no, I have a fine gardener, you see.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.540
See? There he is.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:35.160
That man takes care of everything in here.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.250
His name is Burton, and he's not
a very considerate chap,

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:41.410
but he is quite handy
when it comes to gardening.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:46.790
Through the sweat of those of lower
status, the noble stock blooms.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:51.660
This conservatory is a veritable
microcosm of our society!

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:00.450
I have an idea! How about we have
a tea party here sometime?

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.660
It will feel as though
we are taking in paradise.

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:15.790
What do you think you're doing?

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.750
Who else besides you and me lives here?

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.540
And yet you set places for three.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.120
I had a dream.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:31.580
I dreamt our boy was crying
because he was hungry.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:41.790
Even so, what good will carrying
on this game of house do?!

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:45.870
You're right. No good will come of it.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.660
Nothing at all, now.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:11.250
In light of this being our first class,
how about we end things here?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.200
That was a good lecture, and easy to follow.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:20.830
Still, I can scarcely believe our
new maths professor is so young.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:22.660
Honestly, I'm astounded.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.830
He must surely be quite brilliant.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:38.660
Would you mind if I joined you?

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.580
Who are you?

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.660
The name is William James Moriarty.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:56.500
I recently moved here to teach
mathematics at the university.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:58.950
You're a college professor?

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:02.540
What does a bigwig college professor
like you want with me?

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:07.700
I saw the conservatory at the Viscount
of Belfor's residence the other day.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:11.000
I understand you take care of it for him.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.660
Yeah, that's my job.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:18.700
I expect it is no easy task
to raise so many rare varieties.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:21.410
It is truly stunning.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.580
I'm glad you like it.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.330
Someone with skills such as yours

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:29.120
could put them to use in the botanic
gardens of London, could they not?

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.540
Hmph, what a load of bollocks.
My father, and his father,

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.700
served as gardeners for the viscount here.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:38.160
Which means I do, too.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:44.370
We were born here, and here is where we die.
That's the sort of life we live.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:48.830
That's the sort of life you live, you say?

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:53.910
I heard about your son.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:57.750
It seems your wife's psychological
trauma has not yet healed.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.910
Shouldn't you hurry home to her
and be at her side--?

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:02.910
It's none of your business!

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:11.500
My being there for her does no good at all.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:15.830
She hates the viscount.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:21.200
She also hates me, who was
powerless to do anything

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:24.290
whilst my own son was being condemned to die.

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.660
You were not powerless to do anything.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.290
You simply didn't do anything.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.330
So then...

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:50.910
So then, what was I supposed to have done?

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.830
What can I do to save Michelle?

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.250
I must...

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:20.450
Mr Burton, as it happens,
apart from my maths instruction,

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:24.370
I also run a consultancy business on the side.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:28.250
Unless I miss my guess,
I may be of some service to you.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.580
Brother...

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.540
Have you finished your research?

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:54.200
Yes, I found it.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.450
A way to dispel the darkness.

00:13:56.450 --> 00:14:01.200
Darkness? Are you referring to the viscount?

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.950
No.

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:05.580
I mean the gloom which
resides within one's soul,

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:09.910
compromising the strength it takes
to live their life as a person.

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:15.330
Welcome. I'm pleased you could come.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.870
Today is our tea party in
your vaunted conservatory.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.750
I'm sure it will be most entertaining.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:26.290
I can promise that your expectations
will not be betrayed. Hmm?

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:31.080
Truth be told, we thought it impolite
to simply accept your invitation.

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:35.750
We've come by something rather rare,
so we brought it by way of a gift.

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:48.160
Ho, what is this?

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:52.540
It looks similar to the marmalade I often have.

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:56.290
Oh, please, have a taste first.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.870
All right...

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:10.000
Orange? No, that's not it.
Nor is it lemon. What is it?

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:13.540
You cannot tell what kind of marmalade it is?

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:16.120
It is something you know
quite well, Lord Belfor.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.080
I do?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.910
It is grapefruit.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:21.580
It is?

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:27.450
This is a surprise. I thought that grapefruits
were merely for looking at;

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.870
I never realised they were so delicious.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.080
It appears to be to your liking.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.700
Yes.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:43.450
The slight bitterness to it could
actually become habit-forming.

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:46.040
In that case, the juice is not bad, either.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:50.830
Particularly freshly squeezed. It has a
briskness not to be found elsewhere.

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:59.700
Yes, quite!

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.450
Well, this has been instructive indeed.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.250
Stop! What are you doing?!

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:03.040
Wh-Wh-What is the meaning of this?!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.660
This is for what you did to my son!

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:08.660
You just let my son die!

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.950
That night in the rain!

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:21.160
In retribution, I'll cut your
heart out, right here!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.410
M-My chest!

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:27.450
Lord Belfor, your medicine, quickly.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:38.120
Your lordship, here.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.910
I am ever so sorry, your lordship.

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:51.500
I had no idea my wife would
do something so drastic.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:54.580
Burton!

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:59.620
Spare me your excuses! You're sacked!
Get out of my sight this instant!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:03.250
But hold on tightly to that woman!

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:09.370
I'll let the police--no, I will personally
give her what she has coming!

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.950
That woman...

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:26.450
She pointed a knife at me, of all things!

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:28.750
This is why I can't abide lower-class scum!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:33.000
Lord Belfor, it is bad for
you to get so agitated.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.830
Luckily, you seem to be no worse for wear.

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:38.250
Perhaps you should settle
this amicably with them.

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:41.080
Do you take this for something
I can settle amicably?!

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.750
I swear, that woman will--!

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:46.040
Wh-What was that?

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.450
I suddenly feel faint...

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:53.040
Were you not aware?

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:55.950
The furanocoumarin that grapefruits contain

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:58.950
has a profound influence on
quinine's mechanism of action,

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.580
and causes blood pressure to drop sharply.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:06.370
M-My doctor... Someone call my doctor...

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:12.700
There are those who asked the
very same thing of you, once.

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:18.370
You also gave them an answer at the time.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:22.620
Do you remember what it was?

00:19:31.450 --> 00:19:33.000
You don't mean...

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:36.580
...this was all set up from the beginning...?

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:39.540
So you've finally figured it out, have you?

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:42.080
Michelle!

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:46.370
Michelle, you did well.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:55.580
I contrived all of this at Mr Burton's request.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.290
Why would you do such a thing...?

00:19:58.290 --> 00:20:00.830
This is your punishment.

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:09.700
Delivered to you by James
Moriarty, Crime Consultant.

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.830
With the letter I gave you yesterday,

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:36.910
you should be able to find gardening
work at Queen Mary's Garden.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:42.000
I truly have no idea how I can
ever thank you for this.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:45.500
Not at all. After all you've been through,
no thanks is necessary.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:50.620
Indeed. We did no more
than offer the help you needed.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:55.580
It was something you
carried out all on your own.

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:33.040
Do you suppose Mr Burton and Michelle
will be able to carry on now?

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:36.450
By sharing the burden of their crime,

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:39.250
the two of them have forged
a bond not easily broken.

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:53.330
That will never be lost.

00:22:07.620 --> 00:22:11.290
<i>An oath committed by souls assumed,</i>

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:15.500
<i>with ideals that wallow in genetic karma</i>

00:22:29.500 --> 00:22:34.580
<i>Lie! Be resolute if you're going</i>
<i>to share your pain</i>

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:36.830
<i>(Demonstrate your resolve)</i>

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:40.330
<i>Like, dislike, you can't afford</i>
<i>to care either way</i>

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:43.540
<i>It depends on the objective</i>
<i>(Making it happen is what's most important)</i>

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:47.080
<i>The necessary evil of self-sacrifice</i>

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:50.700
<i>is a righteous cause that no one can comprehend</i>

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:54.450
<i>Take pride in the inviolable bonds shared</i>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:22:59.290
<i>among brothers who bear the same crime</i>

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:02.950
<i>Make a chance trigger your inevitable stance</i>

00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:04.620
<i>and get drunk on your accomplishments</i>

00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:06.410
<i>at the end</i>

00:23:06.410 --> 00:23:09.580
<i>Don't believe in what you can see,</i>

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:13.830
<i>in truths there's no point in knowing</i>
<i>(Whatever it takes)</i>

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:20.410
<i>Defer to its own validity,</i>
<i>you only have one goal</i>

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:21.910
<i>(Let me hear you say)</i>

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:28.750
<i>You can't lie to yourself, come along with me</i>

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:34.410
<i>It's all because there is no answer</i>

00:23:34.410 --> 00:23:36.790
<i>There is no turning back</i>

